jassim is 22 years old and like many  young men his age  enjoys football he is autistic and his  mother says playing the sport in a safe  environment  has improved his life over the last two  years  after finishing school jason and those  like him had no chance to take part in  any activities  so he stayed at home and most of the  time doing nothing but now they come  here and free themselves of any negative  energy  anger or aggressiveness they wait  impatiently for this day every week  this program really grants them their  inherent right to life  and i hope it will run forever  jassim is benefiting from a sports  program here in doha  teaching those with special needs  several sports including football  the ability friendly football program is  a relatively new initiative but it's  already got the backing  of the qatar 2022 world cup organizers  and one of their most famous ambassadors  former australia captain tim cahill does  a lot of work with the world cup social  legacy division  generation amazing comes part and parcel  with who i am as a person  um i've had a great career but one of  the most magical things is  to be able to share my wealth of  knowledge to have fun with the kids  according to britain's national autistic  society physical activity can improve  social skills communication and anxiety  it creates a sense of belonging and it  creates an environment where anyone can  just quite simply be together and play  and it's through that process of having  fun and engaging  that like you see a genuine growth in  people's  ability to communicate and desire to  communicate as well  qatar's world cup organizers are aiming  to make next year's tournament the most  accessible ever  as well as providing dedicated areas for  those with physical disabilities  stadiums will host sensory rooms for  autistic people  to have a quiet space where they can  enjoy the matches  it's all about inclusiveness we talk  about inspiring the next generation and  this is the next generation and  as an ambassador and also as a father i  want to be a part of this  i hope more attention is paid to this  slice of our youth  simply because autistic people are very  intelligent and enjoy  many other talents their talents  wouldn't come to light  unless they're given the choice to  interact with their surroundings  with just over 20 months to go until the  tournament kicks off  the hard work continues to get qatar  ready to host the world cup  while also making it a welcoming  environment for all  joanna gazroska al jazeera dojo
 

